From 18fde081dbf74da3f5c7002c8794e6d49e6ee065 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bjorn Pagen <11238136+bjornpagen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 12:14:03 -0600
Subject: [PATCH v1] Decide a serializable conflict out by the snapshot first

CheckForSerializableConflictOut() is passed the top-level xid of the
transaction that created a tuple version the reader cannot see, or that
deleted one it can.  For a RECENTLY_DEAD or DELETE_IN_PROGRESS version
that the scan cannot see, HeapCheckForSerializableConflictOut() passes
the creator, which is often a transaction whose writes are all in the
reader's snapshot: the version is invisible because its deleter
committed first.  For such an xid there is no rw-antidependency, and
the ordinary path returns at XidIsConcurrent().

Two earlier tests run before that one.  When the xid's SERIALIZABLEXACT
has been summarized, the SLRU lookup either raises "conflict out to old
pivot" or "identification as a pivot, with conflict out to old
committed transaction", or sets SXACT_FLAG_SUMMARY_CONFLICT_OUT on the
reader, which then fails at its next rw-conflict in ("identification as
a pivot, during write").  When it has not been summarized but carries a
summary conflict out, the reader fails with "conflict out to old
pivot".  Both rest on the premise that the reader has a conflict out to
the xid, which a transaction that finished before the snapshot cannot
give it.

Summarization begins once the SERIALIZABLEXACT pool is full of finished
transactions no active one has passed.  One long transaction holding an
xid anywhere in the cluster holds back every snapshot's xmin, and with
it SxactGlobalXmin under overlapping serializable load, and keeps every
version deleted meanwhile RECENTLY_DEAD.  A serializable transaction
with nothing concurrent in its own database then fails with 40001
because of load in other databases.

Test XidIsConcurrent() first, before the SERIALIZABLEXID hash or the
SLRU is consulted, and drop the later duplicate.  For an xid that is
not concurrent this returns exactly what the path without summarization
already returned, with nothing set; every concurrent xid takes the path
it took before.  heapam already discards xids older than TransactionXmin
before calling here; this extends the same rule to the xids between the
snapshot's xmin and xmax that it saw committed.

The isolation test serializable-summarized-conflict-out keeps a
serializable transaction with an xid open, fills the sxact pool until
the writer's first transactions are summarized, and runs both failing
paths; each of its transactions now commits.
---
 src/backend/storage/lmgr/predicate.c          | 17 ++--
 .../serializable-summarized-conflict-out.out  | 57 ++++++++++++++
 src/test/isolation/isolation_schedule         |  1 +
 .../serializable-summarized-conflict-out.spec | 77 +++++++++++++++++++
 4 files changed, 145 insertions(+), 7 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 src/test/isolation/expected/serializable-summarized-conflict-out.out
 create mode 100644 src/test/isolation/specs/serializable-summarized-conflict-out.spec

diff --git a/src/backend/storage/lmgr/predicate.c b/src/backend/storage/lmgr/predicate.c
index 0ae85b7..b09c6c4 100644
--- a/src/backend/storage/lmgr/predicate.c
+++ b/src/backend/storage/lmgr/predicate.c
@@ -3972,6 +3972,16 @@ CheckForSerializableConflictOut(Relation relation, TransactionId xid, Snapshot s
 	if (TransactionIdEquals(xid, GetTopTransactionIdIfAny()))
 		return;
 
+	/*
+	 * A transaction whose writes are in our snapshot is no conflict out,
+	 * whether its details are still in the SSI structures or were summarized
+	 * to the SLRU.  The table AM passes the creator of a version that our
+	 * snapshot sees deleted as well as of one it cannot see at all, so this
+	 * must be decided before either is consulted.
+	 */
+	if (!XidIsConcurrent(xid))
+		return;
+
 	/*
 	 * Find sxact or summarized info for the top level xid.
 	 */
@@ -4065,13 +4075,6 @@ CheckForSerializableConflictOut(Relation relation, TransactionId xid, Snapshot s
 		return;
 	}
 
-	if (!XidIsConcurrent(xid))
-	{
-		/* This write was already in our snapshot; no conflict. */
-		LWLockRelease(SerializableXactHashLock);
-		return;
-	}
-
 	if (RWConflictExists(MySerializableXact, sxact))
 	{
 		/* We don't want duplicate conflict records in the list. */
